After the TypeScript to JavaScript compilation, these functions will still exist and slow down our code (although only by a tiny amount!).

It's potentially worth replacing them with `as <TYPE>` and `as <TYPE> | undefined`, but the syntax is not as nice and the performance impact isn't too big so I'm on the fence, e.g.

```typescript
state = createImperativeState(() => {
  foo: domain.optional<string>("default"),
});
// this is equivalent (but faster)
state = createImperativeState(() => {
  foo: "default" as string | undefined,
});
```

I feel like this will probably be nicer as an ES6 class, e.g. something like:

```typescript
/**
 * Resettable state storage.
 *
 * @example
 * ```
 * // you can use the `domain` functions for easier typing
 * const state = new ImperativeState(() => {
 *   foo: domain.optional<string>("default"),
 *   bar: domain.identity<number[]>([]),
 *   baz: domain.optional(1),
 * });
 *
 * state.records.foo = "hi";
 * console.log(state.records.foo); // prints "hi";
 * state.reset();
 * console.log(state.records.foo); // prints "default";
 *
 * // typeof state.records:
 * // {
 * //   foo: string | undefined, // actual: undefined
 * //   bar: number[],           // actual: []
 * //   baz: number | undefined, // actual: 1
 * // }
 * ```
 */
export class ImperativeState<S extends Record<string, unknown>> {
  init: () => S;
  records: S;

  /**
   * @param init - Function that creates the default state.
   */
  constructor(init: () => S) {
    this.init = init;
    this.records = init();
  }

  reset() {
    Object.keys(this.records).forEach((key) => {
      delete this.records[key];
    });
    Object.entries(this.init()).forEach(
      ([key, value]: [
        keyof S,
        any // eslint-disable-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any
      ]) => {
        this.records[key] = value;
      }
    );
  }
}
```

The behavior will then be exactly the same, but it will match the normal JavaScript/TypeScript code-style that most projects use.

I've also got an example commit at https://github.com/aloisklink/mermaid/commit/35191a611947ff152eaaf849c8d006a387b6dccb that we could push to this branch.

